      "message": "suggestion : use is_valid_ether_addr(tha), which is defined as !is_multicast_ether_addr(addr) \u0026\u0026 !is_zero_ether_addr(addr).\n\nnote - arp_process() is called for all ARP-capable device types, not just Ethernet. is_zero_ether_addr() and is_multicast_ether_addr() unconditionally read ETH_ALEN (6) bytes and require u16 alignment. On a non-Ethernet or virtual/syzkaller netdev with dev-\u003eaddr_len \u003c ETH_ALEN (e.g., addr_len \u003d\u003d 1), arp_rcv() only pulls arp_hdr_len(dev) bytes (tha is dev-\u003eaddr_len bytes followed by 4 bytes of tip), causing an unaligned read and a 1-byte out-of-bounds read past the pulled ARP header.",
