      "message": "ip_rcv_options() unconditionally calls skb_cow(skb, skb_headroom(skb)) (line 281). If skb is cloned (e.g., when tcpdump or an AF_PACKET socket is active) or lacks headroom, skb_cow() calls pskb_expand_head(), which reallocates skb-\u003ehead and frees the old buffer.\n\nSuggested fix: Reload iph \u003d ip_hdr(skb); at the start of the if (in_dev \u0026\u0026 IN_DEV_ORCONF(in_dev, DROP_UNICAST_IN_L2_MULTICAST)) block)\n\n\t\tif (in_dev \u0026\u0026\n\t\t    IN_DEV_ORCONF(in_dev, DROP_UNICAST_IN_L2_MULTICAST)) {\n\t\t\tbool is_dhcp_resp \u003d false;\n\t\t\tiph \u003d ip_hdr(skb);",
